      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "i) Continuous Emission Monitoring System (CEMS)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Continuous emission monitoring system (CEMS) can usually monitor gas like CO, O₃, SO₂, NO₂, VOCs and PM at industrial sites."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "ii) Air Quality Monitoring Stations (AQMS)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Fixed monitoring stations are equipped with various sensors and analyzers to measure pollutant level in real time located in urban areas and industrial zones."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "iii) Remote Sensing Techniques"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Satellites equipped with sensors can measure atmospheric pollutants over large areas, providing valuable data on regional and global air quality."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
